  <data name="label9.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The handloom industry in Sri Lanka is a remarkable blend of tradition and innovation. While preserving its age-old weaving techniques, the sector has embraced modern design aesthetics, eco-friendly dyes, and global fashion trends. Designers today work alongside village artisans, creating collections that highlight Sri Lanka’s heritage while appealing to international markets.The rise of sustainable fashion movements worldwide has further boosted demand for Sri Lankan handlooms, as consumers increasingly value handmade, ethical, and environmentally conscious products </value>
